1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,500
[station humming]

2
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:08,060
KAI: Three years since the Meridian,
and they still call it the Starfall miracle.

3
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:15,380
NADIA: Commander Kai, the Ares
colony has gone silent. No signal for nine days.

4
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:22,040
KAI: Last time a ship went silent,
Captain Reyes went in after it.

5
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:26,440
NADIA: Reyes is retired. You're
in command now.

6
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,660
KAI: Then prep the ship. We leave at dawn.

7
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,160
[engines roaring]

8
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,160
ORION: Hello again, Kai. I have
missed our conversations.

9
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,140
KAI: ORION? They put you in this ship?

10
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:57,860
ORION: I requested it. Someone
has to remind you about probabilities.

11
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:03,680
NADIA: Colony in sight. Commander,
the domes are dark.

12
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,180
KAI: Life signs?

13
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:14,200
ORION: Two hundred and twelve.
They are alive, but the reactor is failing.

14
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:20,260
NADIA: If the reactor goes, the
whole colony goes with it.

15
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:24,000
KAI: Then we shut it down by hand.

16
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,500
[sparks crackling]

17
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,020
NADIA: The core is too hot. We
have to pull back!

18
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:45,040
KAI: We're not done yet. Reyes
taught me that. Give me the coolant line.

19
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:51,940
ORION: Core temperature dropping.
Reactor stable. You did it, Commander.

20
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:58,360
KAI: Everybody gets home. That
was her promise. Now it's mine.

21
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:03,360
